---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import SalesSignup from "../components/SalesSignup.astro";
import PreviewStack from "../components/PreviewStack.astro";
import GitCommitLog from "../components/GitCommitLog.astro";
import GitIntro from "../images/git-intro.png";
import GitCoverFront from "../images/git-cover-front.png";
import GitCoverBack from "../images/git-cover-back.png";
import GitScenario from "../images/git-scenario.png";
import GitCloudCover from "../images/git-cloud-cover.png";
---

<PageLayout multiLineHeader>
  <div>
    <p>
      <em
        >The Fujoshi Guide to Web Development is structured in issues with a
        single learning focus, which are then collected into volumes</em
      >–similarly to a manga or comic. Featured in our first Kickstarter, Volume
      0 collects our inaugural issues introducing Git, GitHub and open source
      development.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="sales">
    <h2>Want your own copy?</h2>
    <SalesSignup tag="volume-0" />
  </div>
  <article class="issue">
    <h2 id="issue-1"><a class="heading-link" href="#issue-1">Issue 1 – Using Git locally</a></h2>
    <div>
      <PreviewStack
        images={[
          { src: GitCoverFront, alt: "Issue 1 cover" },
          { src: GitIntro, alt: "Git's introduction from the guide" },
          { src: GitScenario, alt: "Scenario page from Issue 1" },
          { src: GitCoverBack, alt: "Issue 1 back cover" },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="content">
        <section>
          <h3>In this Issue</h3>
          <p>
            Meet Git and learn his most fundamental commands through a dress-up
            game with his friends CSS, HTML, ARIA, and Boba-tan! Tracking your
            code changes and sorting through different versions of a codebase
            has never been such a breeze–no matter the size of your wardrobe.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h3>Topics</h3>
          <GitCommitLog
            entries={[
              { message: "What is version control (Git)?" },
              { message: "The commit cycle" },
              { message: "Navigating and manipulating code history" },
            ]}
          />
        </section>

        <section class="status">
          <h3>Current status</h3>
          <GitCommitLog
            entries={[
              {
                state: "complete",
                hash: "c001ee",
                type: "release",
                tone: "teal",
                message: "**🎉 Digitally Released to Kickstarter Backers! 🎉**",
              },
              {
                state: "pending",
                type: "release",
                tone: "purple",
                message: "Public release coming 2026",
              },
              {
                state: "pending",
                type: "sales",
                tone: "red",
                message:
                  "Early access for [FujoCoded](https://www.fujocoded.com)'s special events",
              },
            ]}
            variant="status"
          />
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="issue">
    <h2 id="issue-2">
      <a class="heading-link" href="#issue-2">Issue 2 – Version Control in the Cloud (ft. GitHub)</a>
    </h2>
    <div>
      <PreviewStack
        images={[
          {
            src: GitCloudCover,
            alt: "Issue 2 cover: Version Control in the Cloud",
          },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="content">
        <section>
          <h3>In this Issue</h3>
          <p>
            When Boba-tan's laptop dies in the middle of her latest project, Git
            and GitHub team up to save the day! With their powers combined (and
            her code in the cloud), Boba-tan can finally get back to the choice
            that matters: should her shrine feature her blorbo's sexy monster
            form, or his equally sexy human fansona?
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h3>Topics</h3>
          <GitCommitLog
            entries={[
              { message: "Cloning and uploading (pushing) repositories" },
              { message: "Working with branches" },
              { message: "Merging changes" },
              { message: "The pull request process" },
            ]}
          />
        </section>

        <section class="status">
          <h3>Current status</h3>
          <GitCommitLog
            entries={[
              {
                state: "complete",
                hash: "d4af7e",
                type: "draft",
                tone: "teal",
                message: "First draft and beta read completed",
              },
              {
                state: "pending",
                type: "preview",
                tone: "purple",
                message:
                  "**In production:** a (pre)²view for backers (see our [roadmap](/roadmap))",
              },
              {
                state: "pending",
                type: "release",
                tone: "red",
                message: "Digital release to Kickstarter backers",
              },
            ]}
            variant="status"
          />
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <p class="note" id="issue-3">
    <em>Looking for Issue 3?</em> The content originally planned for it has been folded
    into <a href="#issue-2">Issue 2</a>.
  </p>
  <style>
    article {
      width: 100%;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-block: 24px;
    }

    .issue {
      margin-block: 28px;
    }

    .issue h2 {
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .issue > div {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 300px 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
      align-items: start;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .issue > div {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 48px;
        align-items: center;
      }
    }

    .content {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 32px;
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .content h3 {
      font-family: "freude", sans-serif;
      font-weight: 400;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      line-height: 1.1;
      color: var(--terminal-dark);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .content h3::after {
      content: "";
      flex: 1;
      height: 2px;
      border-radius: 1px;
      background: var(--terminal-dark);
      opacity: 0.18;
    }

    .content > section {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 14px;
    }

    .content p {
      margin: 0;
      line-height: 1.55;
      text-wrap: pretty;
    }

    .note {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      opacity: 0.8;
    }

    .sales {
      width: 100%;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 19rem);
      grid-template-areas:
        "title form"
        "desc form"
        "links form";
      grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr;
      column-gap: 40px;
      align-items: start;
      background-color: white;
      padding: 28px 36px 32px;
      border-radius: 16px;
      box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px 0px var(--fujo-red);
      border: 2px solid var(--terminal-dark);
      margin-block: 24px;
    }

    .sales h2 {
      grid-area: title;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      text-wrap: balance;
    }

    .sales :global(.signup) {
      display: contents;
    }

    .sales :global(.signup-description) {
      grid-area: desc;
      text-wrap: pretty;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .sales :global([data-guide-signup]) {
      grid-area: form;
      margin: 0;
      width: 100%;
    }

    .sales :global(.signup-links) {
      grid-area: links;
      align-self: end;
      width: auto;
      margin: 20px 0 0;
      text-align: left;
    }

    .sales :global(.signup-links ul) {
      justify-content: flex-start;
      margin-inline: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .sales {
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        grid-template-areas:
          "title"
          "desc"
          "form"
          "links";
        grid-template-rows: auto;
        text-align: center;
        padding: 28px 24px 30px;
      }

      .sales :global([data-guide-signup]) {
        margin-top: 20px;
        width: min(100%, 32rem);
        justify-self: center;
      }

      .sales :global(.signup-links) {
        text-align: center;
        margin-top: 28px;
      }

      .sales :global(.signup-links ul) {
        justify-content: center;
        margin-inline: auto;
      }
    }
  </style>
</PageLayout>
